  (59, 3, 2, 'What colour is the ink? Ignore what the word says.', 'The word says Orange, but it is printed in Pink ink.', 10, 1),
  (60, 3, 2, 'What colour is the ink? Ignore what the word says.', 'The word says Blue, but it is printed in Green ink.', 10, 1),
  (61, 4, 2, 'Which colour comes next?', 'The pattern repeats every 3 colours: Pink, Pink, Orange.', 30, 1),
  (62, 4, 2, 'Which colour comes next?', 'The pattern repeats every 2 colours: Pink, Green.', 30, 1),
  (63, 4, 2, 'Which colour comes next?', 'The pattern repeats every 2 colours: Blue, Orange.', 30, 1),
  (64, 4, 2, 'Which colour comes next?', 'The pattern repeats every 3 colours: Red, Red, Green.', 30, 1),
  (65, 4, 2, 'Which colour comes next?', 'The pattern repeats every 2 colours: Green, Blue.', 30, 1),
  (66, 4, 2, 'Which colour comes next?', 'The pattern repeats every 4 colours: Orange, Pink, Orange, Purple.', 35, 1),
  (67, 4, 2, 'Which colour comes next?', 'The pattern repeats every 3 colours: Red, Red, Orange.', 30, 1),
  (68, 4, 2, 'Which colour comes next?', 'The pattern repeats every 2 colours: Orange, Blue.', 30, 1),
  (69, 5, 2, 'Use the key to turn these colours into a number.', 'Read each colour in order: Purple = 6, Orange = 1. Together they make 61.', 40, 1),
  (70, 5, 2, 'Use the key to turn these colours into a number.', 'Read each colour in order: Purple = 9, Red = 1, Green = 4. Together they make 914.', 45, 1),
  (71, 5, 2, 'Use the key to turn these colours into a number.', 'Read each colour in order: Orange = 5, Blue = 4. Together they make 54.', 40, 1),
  (72, 5, 2, 'Add up the values of these colours.', '2 + 2 + 9 + 8 = 21.', 50, 1),
  (73, 5, 2, 'Add up the values of these colours.', '6 + 7 + 5 + 7 = 25.', 50, 1),
  (74, 5, 2, 'Use the key to turn these colours into a number.', 'Read each colour in order: Pink = 4, Purple = 2, Green = 8. Together they make 428.', 45, 1),
  (75, 5, 2, 'Use the key to turn these colours into a number.', 'Read each colour in order: Green = 4, Pink = 2. Together they make 42.', 40, 1),
  (76, 5, 2, 'Use the key to turn these colours into a number.', 'Read each colour in order: Blue = 8, Red = 6. Together they make 86.', 40, 1),
  (77, 1, 3, 'No students are lazy. Some lazy people are artists. Which conclusion follows?', 'The artists who are lazy cannot be students, because no students are lazy.', 60, 1),
  (78, 1, 3, 'A train leaves at 9:40 and arrives at 13:15. How long is the journey?', 'From 9:40 to 12:40 is 3 hours, and from 12:40 to 13:15 is 35 minutes.', 60, 1),
  (79, 1, 3, 'In a code, FRIEND is written as HUMJTK. How is CANDLE written in the same code?', 'The letters move forward by 2, 3, 4, 5, 6 and 7 places: C to E, A to D, N to R, D to I, L to R, E to L.', 60, 1),
  (80, 1, 3, 'A is B''s sister. C is B''s mother. D is C''s father. How is A related to D?', 'C is the mother of A and B, and D is C''s father, so A is D''s granddaughter.', 60, 1),
  (81, 1, 3, 'If the day after tomorrow is Sunday, what day was it yesterday?', 'If the day after tomorrow is Sunday, today is Friday, so yesterday was Thursday.', 60, 1),
  (82, 1, 3, 'Pointing to a photo, Neha says: "His mother is the only daughter of my mother." How is Neha related to the man?', 'The only daughter of Neha''s mother is Neha herself, so Neha is the man''s mother.', 60, 1),
  (83, 2, 3, 'Which number comes next?', 'The rule is: the gap grows by 2 each time. So the next number is 32.', 50, 1),
  (84, 2, 3, 'Which number comes next?', 'The rule is: square numbers plus 4. So the next number is 40.', 50, 1),
